Infrastructure lives in `{{ .Vars.group }}/`, one Pulumi stack per directory.

**Preview is your work. Apply is not.** Preview a change, read the diff, and put it in
front of a person — `{{ default "pulumi up" (index .Caps "infra.up.command") }}` is
theirs to run, and nothing here runs it for you. An agent that can apply
infrastructure can destroy a production database while reasoning about a typo.

Secrets reach a stack through `pulumi config set --secret`; a plaintext credential in a
`Pulumi.*.yaml` is a failing check, not a style note.
